{
  "id": "coupled-oscillators",
  "term": "coupled oscillators",
  "definition": "Coupled oscillators are a dynamical model in which multiple rhythmic agents, such as metronomes or people coordinating a beat, influence one another and exchange energy so their timing can adapt and become synchronized. In psychology-related studies of coordination and learning, the model is used to describe how a person's internal sense of beat can interact with sound from others to shape shared tempo.",
